## F. MCP tools (JSON)

**`katana_gdal_catalogue`** (F0)
- In: `{filter?: string, schemas?: boolean}`.
- Out: `{gdal_version, algorithms:[{path:["raster","hillshade"], name:"raster hillshade", description, aliases:[], policy:"safe"|"confirm", url, arguments_schema?}]}`.
- `schemas` is honoured only when the filter leaves 20 algorithms or fewer.

**`katana_gdal_describe`** (F0)
- In: `{algorithm: "raster hillshade"}`.
- Out: `{algorithm:{path, description, url, policy}, arguments:[{name, short_name, aliases, type, required, positional, category, default, choices, min:{value,inclusive}, max:{value,inclusive}, count:{min,max}, dataset:{kinds:["raster"], accepts:["name","object"], sources:["drawing","raster","surface","file"]}, depends_on, exclusion_group, dependency_group, input, output, description}], arguments_schema:<JSON Schema of katana_gdal_run.arguments>, gdal_usage:<GDAL's usage JSON verbatim>}`.
- The JSON Schema is generated from the argument specs:
  - boolean, string (enum from choices), integer and number (minimum or exclusiveMinimum, maximum or exclusiveMaximum), array (minItems, maxItems), default;
  - dataset arguments are described as Source objects.

**`katana_gdal_run`** (F0)
- In:
  - `algorithm`: string;
  - `arguments?`: `{<name>: boolean|string|number|array}`;
  - `tokens?`: `[string]`;
  - `inputs?`: `{<dataset arg>: Source | [Source]}`;
  - `output?`: `{layer:string} | {reference:string} | {file:string, format?:string, overwrite?:boolean} | {surface:string}`;
  - `confirm?`: boolean, default false;
  - `preview?`: boolean, default false.
- `Source` is one of:
  - `{scope:"selection"|"drawing"|"area"|"layers", area?:[x0,y0,x1,y1], layers?:[string], only?:boolean, where?:["TYPE=polyline","PROP=owner:Smith*"]}`;
  - `{raster: integer|string}`;
  - `{surface: string, cell?: number}`;
  - `{file: string, layer?: string}`.
- The tool builds the GDAL line and runs it through the Session. The text reply echoes the line as `> GDAL …` followed by the records.
- Out: `{ok, line, algorithm, inputs:[…], scope:[{arg, matched, used, skipped:{reason:n}}], outputs:[{arg, kind, target, layer?, created?, id?, name?, raster?:{width,height}, file?}], text?, return_code?, warnings:[…], cancelled, seconds}`.
- Hints: destructive and open-world. A Confirm algorithm without `confirm:true` is refused.

**Tools the lanes add**
- `katana_terrain_list` (T0): `{}` → `{surfaces:[{name, triangles, points, bounds, zmin, zmax, source}], rasters:[{id, name, role, width, height, cell, crs, nodata, source, derived_from}]}`.
- `katana_gis_query` (V5): `{sql, scope?, area?, layers?, where?, dialect?}` → `{columns:[…], rows:[{…}], matched, used}`.
- `katana_formats` (I2), with resource `katana://formats`: `{kind?, mode?}` → `{formats:[{driver, long_name, kind, read, write, extensions, vsi, open_options, creation_options}]}`.
- `katana_dataset_info` (D1): `{path, json?, stats?, check?}` → the records as structured data plus GDAL's info JSON.
- `katana_references` (D2): `{action?: "list"|"show"|"hide"|"remove"|"opacity"|"color", id?, value?}` → `{references:[…]}`.
- `katana_import` gains (I3): `layers, where, sql, dialect, area, clip, fields, target_layer, max_features, open_options, crs, source_crs, band, subdataset, max_pixels, name, budget, classes, preview`.
- `katana_export` gains (I4): `scope, area, layers, only, where, layer_name, split_by_layer, append, crs, creation_options, layer_creation_options, text, preview`.

