**How every dialog runs:** it builds its line and runs it through `CommandRunner` (`runVerbLine`). It never calls the library to do the work.

## H. Files, globs, reserved blocks, tests

- **Globbed directories:**
  - `src/katana_io/geo/`
  - `src/katana_interop/geo/` with `include/katana/interop/geo/`
  - `src/katana_cad/geo/` with `include/katana/cad/geo/`
  - `src/katana_app/geo/`
  - `src/katana_app/geo/cli/*.cmake`
  - `src/katana_qt/geo/`
  - `tests/geo/test_*.cpp` (suite `katana_geo_tests`, linking katana_app)
  - `tests/geo/headless/*.cmake`
  - `tests/qt_widgets/geo/*.cpp`
- **Reserved blocks** `// ---- <id>: <name> ----` in:
  - `src/katana_app/geo/verb_table.cpp`
  - `src/katana_app/geo/mcp_geo_tools.cpp`
  - `src/katana_app/geo/bindings.cpp`
  - `src/katana_qt/geo/menu_table.cpp`
  - `docs/geoprocessing.md`
  - `docs/mcp.md`
- **Test names** are sentences.
  - `cli.<family>_<what>`, for example `cli.gdal_buffer_of_a_drawn_line_creates_two_hundred_square_metres`;
  - `qt_<what>_headless`;
  - `qt_widgets.<Suite>.<Case>`;
  - gtest cases in `katana_geo_tests`.
- **Contract pins:** each package pins its algorithm paths and arguments in its own test file with `contract_support.hpp`'s `expectArgument(path, name, ArgType, required)`.
